---
description: /ticket create writes a ticket only and does not implement it
alwaysApply: true
---

`/ticket create` creates a ticket and stops. Read the current code, write how it works and how to implement the request, and leave the product code as it is.

Do this when the user says `/ticket create` or asks to create a ticket. A list of changes in that message is the work for the ticket. It is not permission to edit `src/`, styles, tokens, or design docs.

Follow the usual ticket process. Use the next free `NB-` id, copy `tickets/_template.md`, and set `parent` to `NB-E6` for Phase 2. Start from an up-to-date `phase-2` and use a branch named with the ticket id. Register the id in the NB-E6 epic, `tickets/linear.config.json` `buildOrder`, and the build order in `tickets/README.md`. Set `status` to `Todo`. Leave every acceptance box open. Run `npm run tickets:dry-run`, then `npm run tickets:push`. Commit only the ticket files on the ticket branch. Do not merge that branch.

Before writing the ticket, read the code the request touches. Record that evaluation in the ticket:

- Context names the files and the current behavior
- Problem and repro say what is wrong
- Acceptance criteria come from the request
- Technical notes say where the behavior lives and the concrete way to implement the change. Keep those steps out of the acceptance list
- Out of scope lists what must stay as it is

The ticket is ready to build later. Do not change application code in this step, and do not mark the ticket in progress or done.
